# Dance of the Dead puts a creature card from an opponent's graveyard onto the battlefield under its controller's control,
# and when the Aura leaves the battlefield, that creature's controller sacrifices it. Bot1 Cuts Down Bot2's Ornithopter and
# casts Dance of the Dead on the card in Bot2's graveyard: the Ornithopter enters under Bot1's control. Bot2 Disenchants the
# Aura on its turn, and its leaves-the-battlefield ability has Bot1, the creature's controller, sacrifice the Ornithopter,
# which goes to its owner's graveyard (CR 701.21a, 404.1).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Cut Down
Dance of the Dead
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains
Disenchant
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Cut Down.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Dance of the Dead.Cast(Bot2.Graveyard.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Dance of the Dead)
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Dance of the Dead; Cut Down; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Disenchant
